                <pb facs="0318" n="192" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg192"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">463.00 R 29/166: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Whitehouse</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-02-06T13:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 6,
                                1925—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 6—11:40
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>108. My 75, January 21, 3 p.m. British memorandum was adopted by the Conference
                    this morning, subject to my reservation that I had as yet received no
                    instructions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitehouse</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
